{
  "model": "openai/gpt-5.6-luna",
  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "system",
      "content": "Implement the given digital circuit in synthesizable SystemVerilog.\nReturn only one complete module in a single ```systemverilog code block.\nUse exactly the specified module name and ports. Do not provide a testbench.\nNo includes, preprocessor directives, strings, hierarchical references, extra\nmodules, simulation system tasks, file IO, or attributes. Only $signed,\n$unsigned and $clog2 system functions are permitted. Do not use delays.\nThe independent evaluator will supply all input stimuli and check outputs."
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "\nI would like you to implement a module named TopModule with the following\ninterface. All input and output ports are one bit unless otherwise\nspecified.\n\n - input  a (8 bits)\n - input  b (8 bits)\n - output s (8 bits)\n - output overflow\n\nAssume that you have two 8-bit 2's complement numbers, a[7:0] and b[7:0].\nThe module should add these numbers to produce s[7:0]. Also compute\nwhether a (signed) overflow has occurred.\n\n"
    }
  ],
  "stream": false,
  "provider": {
    "only": [
      "mock-only"
    ],
    "allow_fallbacks": false,
    "require_parameters": true
  }
}
